Response: documented from human-service PATCH /orgs/audiences/{id}, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged. Its full document: GET /v1/platform/services/human.","params":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"Audience ID","type":"string"}],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","nullable":true}},"additionalProperties":false},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"Updated audience","schema":{"truncated":true,"firstChars":"{"type":"object","properties":{"audience":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"orgId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"brandId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"name":{"type":"string"},"nlPrompt":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"description":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"One-sentence summary of who THIS audience targets, distinct from the shared batch nlPrompt. LLM-generated at /suggest time. null for rows predating this field."},"provider":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["apollo","apify","crm",null]},"apolloAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Pointer to the faithful Apollo audience owned by apollo-service ('one filter vocabulary' Wave 2). Set for apollo audiences; null for apify (legacy) rows and pre-Wave-2 rows not yet backfilled. The faithful filters live in apollo-service; the `filters` field below is human-service's opaque cache of them."},"crmUploadId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"The ONE imported CRM source (crm-service upload id) this audience is bound to. When set, every CRM serve made under this audience is restricted to the people that came from that file, so several CRM audiences can coexist for one brand and each behaves as its own audience. null = unbound ⟹ the serve covers the brand's whole imported list (the pre-existing behaviour)."},"crmPeople":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"signedUp":{"type":"boolean"},"replied":{"type":"boolean"},"reachableBy":{"type":"string","enum":["phone","email"]},"segment":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"nullable":true},"description":"A part of the brand's own CRM, as crm-service's PeopleSegment states it (passed through verbatim, validated by crm-service): dealStages [{stage, pipeline?}], dealStatuses, tags, reached / notReached (funnel steps), includeClients, includeOptedOut. Lists OR, keys AND; clients and opted-out people are out unless stated. Names come from crm-service GET /orgs/contacts/segments.","example":{"dealStages":[{"pipeline":"Sales Pipeline","stage":"Form Filled - No Appointment"}]}}},"description":"The PEOPLE-pool filter this CRM audience is bound to: every serve draws from the brand's merged people (everyone its connected tools know, one row per human) who match it, instead of from imported files. null = not people-bound (file-bound via crmUploadId, or the whole imported list)."},"crmPeopleByStage":{"type":"array","nullable":true,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"pipeline":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"stage":{"type":"string"},"served":{"type":"integer"},"remainingSendable":{"type":"integer"},"totalSendable":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["pipeline","stage","served","remainingSendable","totalSendable"]},"description":"A people-bound CRM audience whose segment names dealStages: crm-service's counts per stated stage (same snapshot as Size / Remaining). Entries overlap when a person holds deals at two of them. null otherwise."},"offerId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The offer (Org > Brand > Offer > Campaign) this audience belongs to — an id owned by brand-service. An audience is assembled for one distinct thing the brand sells, so it is scoped to that offer rather than to every offer of the brand. null = no offer stated ⟹ the audience is brand-wide, the pre-existing behaviour."},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["suggested","active","paused","archived","deprecated"],"description":"Always 'suggested' (inactive) for a freshly-suggested audience."},"source":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"profileAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"The client PROFILE (WHO, a cold audience the client keeps or pauses on the Targeting page) this source list was built for: a buying-signal list (hiring now, new in role, recently funded) or a competitor-post engagement list finds THAT profile's people, screened against the profile's text. Pausing or archiving the profile pauses its lists; resuming it resumes them (unless the source itself is off). null on a profile itself, on a whole-ICP list built before profiles had their own (retired once they do), and on every other audience. Show profiles = rows with null here and channels[0].list = apollo_search; sources = channels[0].list."},"role":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["target","search",null],"description":"AUDIENCE-PER-OFFER-1107. 'target' = THE audience of its offer: its text is who the offer targets, it has no list of its own and finds people through the brand's lists, each person judged against its text. 'search' = a list of the brand (Apollo search, signals, engagement) walked by every offer audience of it; hidden from GET /orgs/audiences unless role=search. null = an audience as before."},"canonicalAudienceId":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"format":"uuid","description":"When this audience is a deprecated provider-variant (e.g. retired '<base> [Apify]' from the apify->apollo migration), the id of its active canonical replacement. Membership/stats reads resolve a deprecated match to this audience. null for non-deprecated / unlinked rows."},"filters":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"additionalProperties":{"nullable":true}},"avatarUrl":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"Audience avatar as a hosted HTTP(S) URL. null until generated."},"apolloCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"apifyCount":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"countedAt":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"degraded":{"type":"boolean","description":"The chooser's verdict on the audience it picked for this row: true when no attempt apollo-service explored really answered the request and the least-bad one was chosen anyway. INFORMATION for the customer and the dashboard — nothing here blocks, filters or warns on it, and an audience is always chosen. false for rows created before the flag existed and whenever the chooser judged the pick a genuine answer."},"createdByUserId":{"type":"string"","note":"Narrow the request (a filter, a limit, one id) to read the rest."}}],"needsTheirYes":false}

describe_operation {"operationId":"postV1Replies"} → {"operationId":"postV1Replies","method":"POST","path":"/v1/replies","summary":"Reply to a person in their existing email thread","description":"Send an answer into the email thread a person already has with the brand, from the mailbox and persona that wrote to them (the reply a sales rep would send). Name the person by `email` alone: the thread is found from it. When that person wrote back on several campaigns the answer is 409 `ambiguous_thread` with the `candidates`; call again with one `campaign_id`. Write `body_html` without a signature (the persona's is added). Send `sent_by: "human"` for a reply a person decided on. Name the organization with `brandId` or `orgId`. To send files, list offer documents in `attachments` [{ document_id }] (up to 5, 10 MB together; ids from `GET /v1/brands/{id}/offers/{offerId}/documents`): each goes as a real email attachment, and any problem refuses the whole reply, nothing sent (404 `attachment_not_found`, 422 `attachment_too_large` or `attachments_unsupported_on_transport`, 502 `attachment_unavailable`). Pass-through to instantly-service POST /orgs/replies: refusals come back unchanged with a `code` (409 `ambiguous_thread`, `no_reply_to_thread`, `human_took_over`; 404 `campaign_not_found` when the org never emailed that person). The full body is documented from instantly-service.

Request body: documented from instantly-service POST /orgs/replies, which owns and validates it; the gateway forwards it unchanged.

Response: documented from instantly-service POST /orgs/replies, which owns it; the gateway forwards it unchanged. Its full document: GET /v1/platform/services/instantly.","params":[],"body":{"type":"object","properties":{"campaign_id":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"Logical campaign id — the same key manual qualifications and opt-outs use. OPTIONAL: omit it and the thread is found from `email` alone. A thread is a campaign of this org in which the prospect wrote back. Exactly one → the reply goes into it. Several → 409 `ambiguous_thread` listing each candidate (`campaign_id` + `last_message_at`); call again naming one. None but we did email them → 409 `no_reply_to_thread`. Never emailed by this org → 404 `campaign_not_found`. When given, it is used as-is."},"email":{"type":"string","format":"email","description":"The prospect who replied. Matched case-insensitively. Enough on its own to find the thread when `campaign_id` is omitted."},"body_html":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"description":"The answer, HTML. Signed by this service with the sending account's persona — do NOT include a signature."},"sent_by":{"type":"string","enum":["human","automation"],"description":"Who asked for this answer to be sent. Only an `automation` reply goes through the hand-over and stated-not-to-brand gates; a `human` reply never does. A person's earlier hand reply on the thread never refuses an automated one: it stays in the conversation the responder reads. Absent resolves to `automation`; a human surface declares `human` explicitly."},"attachments":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"document_id":{"type":"string","format":"uuid","description":"An offer document id (UUID) from brand-service, of THIS org (x-org-id)."}},"required":["document_id"]},"maxItems":5,"description":"Offer documents to attach to the reply as real files (a case study, a one-pager). This service reads each one from brand-service, bytes included, as this org, and attaches it under brand-service's filename and type. Up to 5, 10 MB together. FAIL LOUD, nothing sent: unknown or another org's document = 404 `attachment_not_found`; over the limits = 422 `attachment_too_large`; brand-service unreadable = 502 `attachment_unavailable`; a thread on the Instantly pipe (no attachment support) = 422 `attachments_unsupported_on_transport`. Absent or empty = the reply exactly as before. Replies only: cold sequence steps never carry a file."}},"required":["email","body_html"],"example":{"campaign_id":"c1a2b3c4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001","email":"alice@media.com","body_html":"<p>Great — how does Thursday 3pm look?</p>","sent_by":"automation"}},"answers":[{"status":"200","description":"The reply was sent (instantly-service shape)","schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"success":{"type":"boolean","enum":[true]},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["sent"]},"reply":{"type":"object","properties":{"transport":{"type":"string","enum":["instantly","smtp"],"description":"Which pipe carried the reply — the one that carried the outreach"},"instantlyCampaignId":{"type":"string"},"leadEmail":{"type":"string"},"accountEmail":{"type":"string","description":"The mailbox that answered. Resolved by this service, never supplied by the caller."},"from":{"type":"string","description":"The From header as the prospect sees it, persona included"},"subject":{"type":"string","description":"The conversation's own subject under `Re:`"},"cc":{"type":"string","description":"The agency inbox this reply was CC'd to — VISIBLE to the prospect, so a reply-all reaches a human. Never a BCC."},"messageId":{"type":"string","description":"Instantly's email id, or the RFC 5322 Message-Id we sent"},"inReplyTo":{"type":"string","description":"The prospect message this reply threads onto"},"attachments":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"documentId":{"type":"string","description":"The brand-service offer document id"},"filename":{"type":"string"},"contentType":{"type":"string"},"sizeBytes":{"type":"integer"},"md5":{"type":"string","description":"Hex md5 of the exact bytes attached"}},"required":["documentId","filename","contentType","sizeBytes","md5"]},"description":"The files this reply carried. Absent when it carried none."}},"required":["transport","instantlyCampaignId","leadEmail","accountEmail","from","subject","cc","messageId","inReplyTo"]}},"required":["success","status","reply"]}}],"needsTheirYes":{"why":"Sends a reply to a person in their email thread.","because":["sends_to_person"],"notNeededWhen":[]}}

